2 CONT * https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Guadalete The Battle of Guadalete was the first major battle of the Umayyad conquest of Hispania, fought in 711 at an unidentified location in what is now southern Spain between the Christ
2 CONC ian Visigoths under their king, Roderic, and the invading forces of the Muslim Umayyad Caliphate, composed mainly of Berbers and some Arabs[1] under the commander Ṭāriq ibn Ziyad. The battle was significant as the culmination of a
2 CONC  series of Berber attacks and the beginning of the Umayyad conquest of Hispania. 
