1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Garc%C3%ADa_I_de_Le%C3%B3n
2 CONT
2 CONT García I de León (c. 870-914) fue el primer rey de León, entre 910 y 914, e hijo de Alfonso III el Magno, rey de Asturias, y de la reina Jimena de Asturias.
2 CONT
2 CONT Fue hermano de los reyes Ordoño II y Fruela II de León, quienes le sucedieron en el trono leonés al haber fallecido García I sin dejar descendencia.
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT García I (c. 871–914) was the king of León from 910 until his death and eldest of three succeeding sons of Alfonso III the Great by his wife Amulina (later called Jimena).
2 CONT
2 CONT García took part in the government alongside his father until 909. In that year was discovered a conspiracy which implicated García. Alfonso renounced the throne and divided the realm between his three sons. León went to García, G
2 CONC alicia to Ordoño, and Asturias to Fruela. Asturian primacy was nevertheless recognised.
2 CONT
2 CONT García's reign saw the fortification of the Duero and the repopulation of Roa, Osma, Clunia, and San Esteban de Gormaz. During this period, the count of Castile gained influence through these endeavours.
2 CONT
2 CONT At his death in Zamora he had no heirs and his kingdom passed to Ordoño.
2 CONT
2 CONT [source: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Garc%C3%ADa_I_of_Le%C3%B3n]
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT García I of León
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT García I (c. 871–914) was the king of León from 910 until his death and eldest of three succeeding sons of Alfonso III the Great by his wife Amulina (later called Jimena).
2 CONT
2 CONT García took part in the government alongside his father until 909. In that year was discovered a conspiracy which implicated García. Alfonso renounced the throne and divided the realm between his three sons. León went to García, G
2 CONC alicia to Ordoño, and Asturias to Fruela. Asturian primacy was nevertheless recognised.
2 CONT
2 CONT García's reign saw the fortification of the Duero and the repopulation of Roa, Osma, Clunia, and San Esteban de Gormaz. During this period, the count of Castile gained influence through these endeavours.
2 CONT
2 CONT At his death in Zamora he had no heirs and his kingdom passed to Ordoño.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT García I de León (c. 870 - 914). Primer rey de León (910 - 914). Fue hijo de Alfonso III el Magno, rey de Asturias, y de la reina Jimena de Asturias. Fue hermano de los reyes Ordoño II y Fruela II de León, quienes le sucedieron en
2 CONC  el trono leonés, al haber fallecido García I sin dejar descendencia.
