2 CONT '''MUNIO Muñoz''', son of MUNIO Rodríguez & his first wife Jimena Ordóñez (-after 20 Oct 1086).  "Monnium Monnuz et uxor sua Uelasquita Monnuz" sold "in territorio Umania villa...Miraualles", which had belonged to "pater nostro do
2 CONC mnum Monnum Ruderiquiz et...mater nostra domna Scemena", to the “Froila Menediz et uxor vestre Maria” by charter dated 13 Mar 1072[871].  Alfonso VI King of Castile granted "illo castello [de Ulver]" to "Munnu Munizi" by charter d
2 CONC ated 4 Dec 1080[872].  "Monnio Moniz, uxor sua Velasquita, Xemena Moniz, Petro Velaz, Sol Sancxiz…" subscribed the charter dated 1 Oct 1085 under which "Gelvira Petriz…cum viro meo…Godino Citiz" donated property in Priaranza to th
2 CONC e monastery of San Pedro de Montes[873].  “...Monniu Monniuz...” confirmed the charter dated 20 Oct 1086 under which “Cotina Uermutiz” donated “Uilla Abduz in loco...Aratoi mea racione...eredavit de viro meo Petro Monniuz et per m
2 CONC eas arras” to Sahagún[874]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' VELASQUITA Muñoz, daughter of MUNIO --- & his wife --- (-after 1 Oct 1085).  "Monnium Monnuz et uxor sua Uelasquita Monnuz" sold "in territorio Umania villa...Miraualles", which had belonged to "pater nostro domnum Monnum 
2 CONC Ruderiquiz et...mater nostra domna Scemena", to the “Froila Menediz et uxor vestre Maria” by charter dated 13 Mar 1072[875].  "Monnio Moniz, uxor sua Velasquita, Xemena Moniz, Petro Velaz, Sol Sancxiz…" subscribed the charter date
2 CONC d 1 Oct 1085 under which "Gelvira Petriz…cum viro meo…Godino Citiz" donated property in Priaranza to the monastery of San Pedro de Montes[876]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Munio & his wife had [three] children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1.         [PEDRO Muñoz (-[22 Aug 1092/7 Feb 1093]). 
2 CONT * 2.         [MUNIO Muñoz (-[17 Jan 1097/21 Mar 1097]).  The dating clause of a charter dated 17 Jan 1097, under which "Vermudo Godestez" donated property in Rimor to the monastery of San Pedro de Montes, names "Monnio Monniz impe
2 CONC rante ipsa terra de Ulver"[879].  His supposed sister "Xemena Munniz" is named in dating clauses of charters of the same monastery, both before the date of this document and from 21 Mar 1097 (see above).
2 CONT * 3.         [JIMENA Muñoz ([1055/65]-Espinareda del Bierzo 1128, after 25 May, [maybe 23 Jul], bur San Andres de Espinareda).  The precise parentage of Jimena Muñoz has been the subject of considerable debate over recent years.  
2 CONC … Mistress: ([1081/82]-) of ALFONSO VI King of Castile and León,
2 CONT
