1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://books.google.cat/books?id=A0GeFRE3QqQC&printsec=frontcover&hl=ca#v=onepage&q&f=false
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Nunilo Jimena
2 CONT Nunilo Jimena. Navarra, s. IX – ?, 924 ant. Reina de Asturias (910-923).
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Consorte
2 CONT Rey, reina de Asturias
2 CONT
2 CONT Biografía
2 CONT Llamada Nunilona Jimena por Enrique Flórez, quien la hace hija del rey navarro, Sancho Garcés y de doña Toda, atribución que ya rechazó Armando Cotarelo al considerarla incompatible con las genealogías navarras. Se sabe con seguri
2 CONC dad que sí es de ascendencia navarra, sobre todo por su nombre, tal como defiende Pérez de Urbel, y que es la esposa del más tarde rey de León, Fruela II, junto con quien participó, en el año 910, en la ofrenda que hicieron a la i
2 CONC glesia ovetense de San Salvador de una preciada arqueta y, dos años más tarde, en la confirmación por ambos reyes a la misma iglesia de sus anteriores privilegios y dádivas.
2 CONT
2 CONT No llegó, en cambio, a ser reina de León, lo fue sólo de Asturias, pues falleció antes de 924, fecha en que su marido, Fruela, comenzó a reinar en León. [...]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT -https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nunilo_Jimena
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------
2 CONT
2 CONT Nunilo Sánchez de Pamplona
2 CONT
2 CONT b. circa 904?
2 CONT
2 CONT Father	Sancho I Garcés, rey de Pamplona1 b. circa 881?, d. 11 October 925
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother	Toda Aznárez de Larraun1 b. circa 885, d. after 970
2 CONT
2 CONT Charts	Descendants of Charlemage
2 CONT
2 CONT      Nunilo Sánchez de Pamplona was daughter of Toda of Aragon & Sancho I of Navarre.1 Also called Nunila Ximena de Navarre.1 She was born circa 904? At Pamplona, Navarre. She was the daughter of Sancho I Garcés, rey de Pamplona a
2 CONC nd Toda Aznárez de Larraun.1 Nunilo Sánchez de Pamplona married rey de Asturias y de León Fruela II Alfonsez "el Leproso", son of Alfonso III "el Magno", rey de Asturias and Jimena Garcés de Navarra; His 1st. 1st cousins.2,1 Nunil
2 CONC o Sánchez de Pamplona was buried in the Church of Saint Mary, Oviedo, Asturias, Iberian peninsula. Reburied to avoid destruction of her tomb by the army of Almanzor. She was laid to rest with her husband, King Fruela II, in the se
2 CONC cond coffin to the left.3
2 CONT
2 CONT Family
2 CONT
2 CONT rey de Asturias y de León Fruela II Alfonsez "el Leproso" b. circa 873, d. circa 925
2 CONT
2 CONT Children	
2 CONT
2 CONT Aznar Froilaz de León+ 1
2 CONT
2 CONT Ordoño Froilaz "el Ciego"+ d. c 9404
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT
2 CONT [S682] D.S.O. Lt.-Col. W. H. Turton, Turton, pg. 46.
2 CONT
2 CONT [S187] Royal Genealogy Database, online http://www.dcs.hull.ac.uk/public/genealogy/
2 CONT
2 CONT [S1074] Bishop Pelayo "the Fabulist" of Oviedo, "CRL", 79.
2 CONT
2 CONT [S682] D.S.O. Lt.-Col. W. H. Turton, Turton, pg. 65.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Jimena Nunilo
2 CONT
2 CONT Alodia Jimena (? - Before November 25 of 913 ). Queen consort of Asturias by marriage to the king Fruela the Leper , king of Asturias and later de León , son of Alfonso III , King of Asturias .
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the mother of Alfonso Froilaz "the Hunchback" , King of Leon .
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Is unknown date of birth. Father Enrique Flórez said Jimena Nunilo Queen was the daughter of King Sancho II of Pamplona and his wife, Queen All Aznar . However, this affiliation has been disproved by several modern historians, who
2 CONC  point out that the queen All Aznar was the wife of Sancho I of Pamplona , not Sancho II. They also note that even the king Sancho Garcés I might be the father of Queen Nunilo Jimena, because it does not appear in the documents of
2 CONC  the time, nor in the Codex de Roda . On the other hand, other authors state that it was daughter of king Jimeno Garcés of Navarre and his wife, Sancha Aznárez.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jimena Nunilo married before the year 911 , with the king Fruela of Asturias , in the year 910 both donated to the Cathedral of San Salvador de Oviedo 's Box of Agates , a relic casket covered with plates of gold and agate and con
2 CONC sidered, together with the Cross of the Angels , the Victoria Cross and the casket of St. Gennadius , one of the four peaks in the gold works Romanesque Asturias. In the sill of the casket containing the names of donors.
2 CONT
2 CONT On November 25 of the 913 confirmed a document which his wife made a donation to the Cathedral of San Salvador de Oviedo .
2 CONT
2 CONT Exact date is unknown death, although several sources say the queen should Nunilo Jimena before the day he died November 25 in the year 913 , because on that day his name appeared on a document issued by her husband.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her husband contracted a second marriage and later in the year 924 , after the death of his brother Leon Ordoño II was proclaimed King of Leon .
2 CONT
2 CONT [ edit ]Sepultura
2 CONT
2 CONT It is unknown where the queen was buried after his death Nunilo Jimena, but in the year 986 the remains of the queen and her husband, the Leper Fruela II , were taken in order of Bermudo II the Gouty , the City of Oviedo in order 
2 CONC to prevent them from being desecrated by Muslim troops led by Mansur . The remains of the king and his wife were deposited in the Pantheon of the kings of the chapel of Nuestra Señora del Rey Casto of the Cathedral of Oviedo . Lat
2 CONC er, King Alfonso V repopulated the city of León , and moved to her most of the remains of the kings that his father, King Bermudo II, had led to Oviedo , but in the pantheon of the church of Nuestra Mrs. King remained Casto Fruela
2 CONC  II's remains and those of his first wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT However, due to the reconstruction of the Pantheon of the kings of the Cathedral of Oviedo , carried out in the early eighteenth century , it would be impossible at present the identification and isolation of the mortal remains of
2 CONC  Queen Nunilo Jimena, who is among the individuals buried there.
2 CONT
2 CONT [ editing ]and offspring Nuptials
2 CONT
2 CONT The result of her marriage to King Fruela the Leper , king of Asturias and later de Leon , a son:
2 CONT
2 CONT Alfonso Froilaz (¿?-¿ 932 ?). King of León and Galicia . In the year 932 , together with their brothers Ordoño and Ramiro, and also with Alfonso IV the Monk , was captured and blinded by order of her cousin, King Ramiro II of León
2 CONC  . His remains were transferred, by order of Alfonso V of León , the Basilica of San Isidoro de León .
2 CONT
