1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Gómez Pérez de Toledo, II=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Fernán Gómez de Toledo and Teresa Vasques da Cunha, Señora de Villaverde 
2 CONT * Integrante de una noble familia mozarabe de la ciudad de Toledo.
2 CONT * Gomez Perez de Guzman de Toledo, Mayor of Toledo was born circa 1308 at of Toledo, Castile, Spain. He married Teresa Garcia de Toledo, daughter of Diego Garcia de Toledo, 3rd Senor de Magan, Senor de Mejorada and Maria Garcia Gu
2 CONC diel, circa 1332. Gomez Perez de Guzman de Toledo, Mayor of Toledo died after 29 June 1340
2 CONT * [http://www.thepeerage.com/p21205.htm '''The Peerage''']
2 CONT * [https://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p802.htm#i24073 '''Our Royal, Titled, Noble, and Commoner Ancestors & Cousins''']
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married: '''Teresa García de Toledo,''' daughter of Diego Garcia de Toledo and María Gudiel 
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''D. Diego Gómez de Toledo, I señor de Casarrubios y Valdepusa;''' Senior notary of the Kingdom of Toledo and mayor of the city.
2 CONT * '''Gutierre Gómez, maestre de Alcántara;''' Prior of the Order of San Juan and master of Alcántara.
2 CONT * '''Pedro Suárez de Toledo el Mozo''' Pastry chef to King Pedro I
2 CONT * '''Suer Gómez de Toledo,''' archbishop of Compostela.
2 CONT * '''Teresa Vázquez,''' married to García Fernández Manrique
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[http://dbe.rah.es/biografias/60570/gomez-perez-de-toledo Gómez Pérez de Toledo]
2 CONT
2 CONT Pérez de Toledo, Gómez. Toledo, c . 1300 - 1352. Pedro I's main pantry and mayor of Toledo.
2 CONT
2 CONT First-born of the marriage formed by Fernán Gómez de Toledo, deprived of the regent queen María de Molina and Fernando IV, senior notary of the Kingdom of Toledo, and Teresa Vázquez de Acuña, nurse of the future king Pedro I. Due 
2 CONC to family influence, the men of the lineage entered the service of the infant's house, occupying high court offices during the reign of Pedro I. His brothers were Gutierre Fernández de Toledo, senior guard and chief pastry chef, P
2 CONC edro Suárez de Toledo, chief waiter of the King, and the archbishop of Toledo Vasco Fernández.
2 CONT
2 CONT His political life began in the municipality in 1322, serving as mayor of the city. He was a vassal of Juan son of the infant Juan Manuel, who favored him with a donation of 10,000 maravedís to rebuild his manor houses in the coll
2 CONC ation of San Antolín de Toledo. Ten years later, he was settled in the Court of Alfonso XI and was armed, along with his brothers, a knight of the Order of the Royal Band of Castile, during the coronation of the King in Burgos.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was part, along with his relatives, of the house of the Infante Pedro, and was appointed, in the accession of the King to the Throne, major butler, charged as such to collect the King's yantares that were pending, so necessary 
2 CONC for the budgetary balance of the royal house. He held the office for two years, since he died in 1352, being buried in the family funeral chapel of the disappeared parish of San Antolín de Toledo.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Teresa Alfón, daughter of Diego García de Toledo, his father's companion, also private and ambassador of Fernando IV and mayor of Toledo; had a numerous offspring. His sons were Diego Gómez de Toledo, senior notary of t
2 CONC he Kingdom of Toledo and mayor of the city; Pedro Suárez de Toledo el Mozo , pastry chef to King Pedro I; Gutierre Gómez de Toledo, prior of the Order of San Juan and master of Alcántara, and Suer Gómez de Toledo, archbishop of Co
2 CONC mpostela.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources and bibliography: Royal Academy of History, Salazar y Castro Collection , C-6, fol. 511; C-7, fol. 56; O-6, fol. 128; M-20, fol. 224; Archive of Santo Domingo el Real de Toledo, docs. 582 and 1238.
2 CONT
2 CONT L. Salazar y Castro, Index of the Glories of the House of Farnese , vol. II, Madrid, Francisco del Hierro, 1716, vol. II, p. 588 [ed. facs., Ollobarrem (Navarra), Wilsen, 1997]; C. Rosell (ed.), "Chronicle of Alfonso the Eleventh"
2 CONC , in Chronicles of the Kings of Castile , Madrid, Atlas, 1953, p. 236; S. Moxó, "Castilian political society in the time of Alfonso XI", in Cuadernos de Historia , 6 (1975), p. 473; L. Vicente Díaz Martín, The officers of Pedro I 
2 CONC of Castilla , Valladolid, University, 1987, pp. 81-82; P. Molenat, Campagnes et Monts de Tolède du xiie au xve siècle , Madrid, Casa de Velázquez, 1997, pp. 333 and 369; B. Martínez Cabiró, "Doña Inés de Ayala", inToletum, Bulleti
2 CONC n of the Royal Academy of Fine Arts and Historical Sciences of Toledo (2002), pp. 115-117; J. Valdeón Baruque, Pedro I and Enrique de Trastamara , Madrid, Aguilar, 2002, p. 57.
2 CONT
2 CONT Pilar Morollón Hernández
2 CONT
