2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00106653&tree=LEO
2 CONT
2 CONT Sancho was the second son of Garcia I Iñiguez, king of Pamplona, and his wife Uracca. He was likely the _Sancium regem_ named as son-in-law _(generum meum)_ by Galindo I Aznár, conde de Aragón, in 867. He is also probably the Sanc
2 CONC ho, lord of Pamplona and head of the Basques, who defeated Muzaffar ibn Muza ibn Di al-Nun at some date between 865 and 875 (during his brother's captivity), as reported by the chronicler Ibn Khaldun. Chronicler Al-Udri names Vela
2 CONC squita, wife of Mutarrif ibn Musa ibn Qasi, as daughter of sahib Sancho, although Ibn Hayyan reports her as daughter of Garcia Iñiguez. Sancho's son Aznár Sánchez married a daughter of his uncle king Fortún Garcés and had a son Sa
2 CONC ncho and two future queens Toda Aznárez, wife of Sancho I Garcés, king of Navarre, and Sancha Aznárez, wife of Sancho's brother, king Jimeno Garcés.
2 CONT
2 CONT It is not recorded when Sancho died.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT < [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Galindo_Aznárez_I Wikipedia] > Galindo Aznárez I (died 867) was Count of Aragón from 844 to 867.
2 CONT
2 CONT Galindo Aznárez and an unknown woman had a son, Aznar Galíndez II, his successor. He appears to have had at least one additional child: an 867 charter mentions a son-in-law, "king Sancho", whom several scholars have identified wit
2 CONC h the younger son of García Íñiguez of Pamplona, Sancho Garcés, father of Aznar Sánchez of Larraun and grandfather of queen Toda of Pamplona.[1][2]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NAVARRE.htm#AssonaIniguez
2 CONT
2 CONT *Íñigo "Arista" & his wife ONECA had four children:
2 CONT **1. GARCÍA Iñíguez ([810]-killed by Arabs [Lumberri] 882[57], bur Leire Monastery). The Codex de Roda names "Garsea Enneconis et domna Assona…et domna ---" m [firstly] URRACA, daughter of ---. García I & his [first] wife had [fou
2 CONC r] children:
2 CONT ***b) SANCHO García . The Codex de Roda names "Fortunio Garseanis et Sanzio Garseanis et domna Onneca" as the children of "Garsea Enneconis" and his unnamed wife[68]. m ---. '''The name of Sancho's wife is not known. Sancho García
2 CONC  & his wife had [two] children''': …
2 CONT ****i) AZNAR Sánchez de Larraún . The Codex de Roda names "Asnari Sanziones qui et Larron" as son of "Sanzio Garseanis"[69]. m (880) [as her second husband,] his first cousin, ONECA [%C3%8D%C3%B1iga] Fortún de Pamplona, [repudiate
2 CONC d wife of ABD ALLAH later ABD ALLAH I Emir of Córdoba], … Aznar Sánchez & his wife had three children: …
2 CONT **** ii)         ['''VELASQUITA''' Sánchez.  Al-Udri records that "Mutarrif ibn Musa" married "Faliskita, hija de Sanyo, señor de Pamplona" and that he brought her to Huesca (which suggests that the marriage should be dated to [87
2 CONC 0/71] when Mutarif took control of Huesca) and had children by her[76].  The date of her marriage is consistent with Velasquita having been the daughter of Sancho, son of García I Iñíguez [King] of Pamplona, but this is not confir
2 CONC med beyond all doubt by the passage in Al-Udri.  m ([871/72]) as his [---] wife, MUTARIF ibn Musa, son of MUSA Ibn Musa & his wife --- (-crucified Córdoba 6 Sep 873).]
2 CONT
2 CONT
