1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Gonçalo Mendes II da Maia , nicknamed The Lidador (c. 1110, Guilhabreu - c. 1139 [ 1 ] ), was a Portuguese aristocrat and knight
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://pt.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gon%C3%A7alo_Mendes_II_da_Maia
2 CONT
2 CONT Gonçalo was the son of Mem Soares da Maia , brother of the magnate and head of the family , Paio Soares da Maia , and of an unknown mother. Being the son of a second son, it was unlikely that he would have close relations with the
2 CONC  head of the family and/or the government of the family estate, but this does not in fact seem to happen.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage
2 CONT
2 CONT Gonçalo is said to have married Gontinha Guterres (before 1110-after 1143), patron saint of the Monastery of Rio Tinto , and who appears to have acquired a considerable amount of property in São João da Madeira [ 1 ] . The couple 
2 CONC had a daughter, Maria Gonçalves, who married Gonçalo Trastamires, her mother's cousin [ 1 ] . Considering the hypothesis that he was still alive in 1159, it is more than likely that Gontinha preceded him in death, given that the l
2 CONC ast document confirming this dates from 1143.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Doubtful chronologies
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT There is no news of this notable baron after 1130. As his two brothers died shortly after the Battle of São Mamede, it is possible to extend Gonçalo's lifetime, at the latest, until 1159 [ 1 ] .
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT "Glorious Death of Gonçalo Mendes da Maia", in a 19th century lithograph.
2 CONT
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id=6000000208928822821&size=large}}
2 CONT
2 CONT Joaquim Pedro de Aragão (1801-?) - Biblioteca Nacional de Portugal - "Morte Gloriosa de Gonçalo Mendes da Maia" Litografia do século XIX, mostrando a morte heróica de Gonçalo Mendes da Maia < [https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Fi
2 CONC le:MorteDeGon%C3%A7aloMendesDaMaia.png link] >
