1 NOTE {geni:about_me} -https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/TOULOUSE%20NOBILITY.htm#BernardGuillaumeMontpellierdied1237
2 CONT
2 CONT 5.       '''  BERNARD GUILLAUME de Montpellier''' (-1237).  In his testament dated 4 Nov 1202, his father bequeathed money for "Bernardium Guillelmum filium meum" to become a canon "Girundæ et Lodoicensem"[902].  Monk at Giron and
2 CONC  Lodève 1202.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' ([after 1213]) JUSIANA de Entenza Señora de Alcolea, daughter of PONCE HUGO de Entenza [Ampurias-Barcelona] & his wife Sibila --- (-after 1213).  The primary source which confirms her parentage and marriage has not yet bee
2 CONC n identified.  Zurita records the marriage of “D. Bernaldo Guillen”, son of “Guillen de Mompeller...y...Doña Ynes”, and “Doña Iusiana, hija de Ponce Ugo hermano del Conde de Ampurias, que por parte de la madre era del linaje de En
2 CONC tença”, arranged by Jaime I King of Aragon who granted him “gran Estado en su Reyno”[903].  The passage is recorded in the paragraph dealing with events in 1213, but the reference to King Jaime (then an infant and only just succee
2 CONC ded to the throne) suggests that the marriage must have taken place later. 
2 CONT
2 CONT  -        CATALONIA NOBILITY. 
