2 CONT
2 CONT Bertha, Queen of Aragon?
2 CONT
2 CONT Agnes, Margravine of Susa
2 CONT
2 CONT Alix, Margravine of Western Liguria
2 CONT
2 CONT House 	House of Poitiers
2 CONT
2 CONT Father 	William VII, Duke of Aquitaine
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother 	Ermensinda
2 CONT
2 CONT Born 	c.1052
2 CONT
2 CONT Died 	after 18 June 1089
2 CONT
2 CONT Agnes of Aquitaine (c.1052 – after 18 June 1089) was a daughter of William VII, Duke of Aquitaine and his wife Ermesinde, who is of unknown origins. Her sister was Clementia, Countess consort of Luxembourg. Agnes herself was Count
2 CONC ess consort of Savoy and possibly Queen consort of Aragon.
2 CONT
