2 DATE ABT 1109
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Wikipedia: [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alfonso_VI_of_Le%C3%B3n_and_Castile#Beatrice Alfonso VI of León and Castile: Beatrice]'''
2 CONT >Alfonso VI married his fifth wife, Beatrice, probably in the first months of 1108.[79][134] Both appear together for the first time on 28 May 1108 in Astorga Cathedral and then in two other royal charters: on 1 January 1109 in th
2 CONC e Cathedral of León and for the last time on 25 April of the same year in Oviedo Cathedral,[134] about three months before the death of the king. According to Bishop Pelagius of Oviedo, once a widow, Beatrice returned to her homel
2 CONC and.[79] Salazar y Acha suggests that she was the daughter of William VIII, Duke of Aquitaine and his third wife Hildegarde of Burgundy,[135] and that she remarried Elias I, Count of Maine.[91][136]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''fr.Wikipédia: [https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alphonse_VI_(roi_de_Le%C3%B3n)#Mort_et_enterrement Alphonse Vi (roi de Léon)]'''
2 CONT >La dépouille mortelle du roi est déposée dans un sépulcre en pierre, au pied de l'église, jusqu'au règne de Sanche IV de Castille (1284-1295), qui juge inconvenant que son ancêtre soit enterré au pied de l'église, et ordonne que 
2 CONC le tombeau soit placé dans le transept de l'église, près de celui de '''Béatrice''' (✝ 1283), fille de l'infant Frédéric de Castille (✝ 1277), exécuté sur ordre de son frère, le roi Alphonse X de Castille[70].
2 CONT
2 CONT '''it.Wikipedia: [https://it.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alfonso_VI_di_León#Beatrice_di_Borgogna Alfonso VI di León: Beatrice di Borgogna]'''
2 CONT >Come riporta il Chronicon Regum Legionensium, la quinta moglie fu Beatrice[77], di origini francesi, come riportato sia dal Recueil des historiens des Gaules et de la France[49]. Anche Reilly riporta che la quinta moglie fu Beatr
2 CONC ice che Alfonso VI sposò, probabilmente nei primi mesi del 1108 e dai documenti da lui consultati risulta essere di origini francesi, probabilmente della casa di Borgogna[102]. Secondo il Diccionario biográfico español, Real Acade
2 CONC mia de la Historia, Beatrice compare citata in un solo documento datato 28 maggio 1108[103].
