2 CONT ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT < [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Garc%C3%ADa_Sánchez_I_of_Pamplona Wikipedia] > García Sánchez I of Pamplona
2 CONT
2 CONT García married his first cousin Andregoto Galíndez, daughter of Galindo Aznárez II, Count of Aragon and his wife Sancha Garcés.[g] Given that Galindo Aznárez II did not have any legitimate male heirs,[24] the rights to the County 
2 CONC of Aragon passed down to Andregoto, and then to her first son with García Sánchez, as a county within the Kingdom of Pamplona.[h]
2 CONT
2 CONT The following children were born of this marriage:
2 CONT # Sancho II of Pamplona, King of Pamplona and Count of Aragon until his death in 994. He was married to his first cousin, Urraca Fernández, daughter of Fernán González of Castile, Count of Castile and his wife Sancha Sánchez, who 
2 CONC was Sancho's paternal aunt.[25]
2 CONT # Toda Garcés[i]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Andregoto was repudiated by her husband in 942.[25] She retired to her lands in Aibar where she died sometime after June 971.[j]
