1 NOTE {geni:about_me} don NUÑO Pérez de Lara, son of don PEDRO González de Lara & his wife doña Eva --- (-killed Cuenca 3 Aug 1177, bur Perales, Cistercian Abbey).  “Comes Malricus…cum fratribus et sororibus nostris Albar Petriz et Nun 
2 CONC Petriz, comitissa domna Elvira, Mari Petriz, Milia Petriz” conferred rights on San Juan de Tardajos by charter dated 31 Jan 1147[1061].  Alférez of Alfonso VII King of Castile Mar 1145 to 4 Feb 1155.  "Aldefonsus…tocius Hyspanie i
2 CONC mperator…cum uxore mea imperatrice domna Rica et…filiis meis Sanctio et Ferrando regibus" donated property to the abbey of Silos by charter dated 28 Oct 1155, confirmed by "…Nunnus Petriz tenens Montor…"[1062].  Conde 11 Mar 1162.
2 CONC   The Annales Compostellani record the capture in 1177 of Cuenca and the death there “III Non Aug” of “Comes Nunius”[1063].  The Anales Toledanos record the death in Jun 1177 of “el Conde D. Nuño”[1064]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT m (before 1147) as her first husband, doña TERESA Fernández de Traba, daughter of don FERNANDO de Traba Conde de Trastámara [& his wife doña Sancha González] ([1130/35]-León 7 Feb 1180, bur León, monastery of San Isidoro).  Accord
2 CONC ing to Barton[1065], doña Teresa was don Fernando's illegitimate daughter by his mistress Queen Teresa of Portugal.  This appears to be based only on the early 17th century work by Prudencio de Sandoval which records a donation da
2 CONC ted 1131 by “la condesa Loba” to the monastery of San Martín de Joyba which names “comes Fredenandus Petri filius comitis Petri…cum filia mea nata regina dona Tereyxa”[1066].  As noted below, it is likely that Queen Teresa was bey
2 CONC ond child-bearing age when she started her relationship with Fernando Pérez de Traba.  Another difficulty is the fact that Teresa gave birth to her children by King Fernando in [1178/80].  It is unlikely therefore that she was bor
2 CONC n earlier than [1130/35].  Queen Teresa, however, died in 1130, by which time she would definitely have been beyond child-bearing age.  If this estimated birth date of Teresa is correct, it is likely that she was one of Fernando´s
2 CONC  youngest children.  Teresa became the mistress of don Fernando II King of León in [1178] and married him as his second wife in Aug 1179. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Teresa Fernández de Traba
2 CONT
2 CONT b. circa 1154, d. 7 February 1180
2 CONT
2 CONT Father	Fernando Pérez de Traba b. circa 1100
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother	Sancha González b. circa 1131
2 CONT
2 CONT      Teresa Fernández de Traba was born circa 1154 at Lara. She was the daughter of Fernando Pérez de Traba and Sancha González. Teresa Fernández de Traba married Ferdinand II , rey de León, son of Alfonso VII "el Emperador", Rey 
2 CONC de Galicia, de León y de Castilla and Berenguela Raimundo de Barcelona, in August 1179; His 2nd. Teresa Fernández de Traba died on 7 February 1180 at Leon, Spain.1
2 CONT
2 CONT Family
2 CONT
