2 CONT # William "Rufus" (c. 1056 – 1100), King of England.
2 CONT # Agatha (c. 1064 – 1079), betrothed to Alfonso VI of Castile.
2 CONT # Constance (c. 1066 – 1090), married Alan IV Fergent, Duke of Brittany; poisoned, possibly by her own servants.
2 CONT # Adela (c. 1067 – 1137), married Stephen, Count of Blois.
2 CONT # Henry "Beauclerc" (1068–1135), King of England, married Edith of Scotland, daughter of Malcolm III, King of the Scots. His second wife was Adeliza of Leuven.
