2 CONT    Roots: Duke of Normandy and King of England.   Descents: William I, the Conqueror, King of England, died 1087.   AIS: William the Conqueror, King of England, born 14 Oct. 1024, Falaise, France; died 9 Sept. 1087, Hermenbraville
2 CONC , France.   Crowned King of England Dec. 25, 1066, after the Battle of Hastings. Reigned from 1066-1087, first of the English Royal House of Normandy.   Davis: William the Conqueror, Duke of Normandy 1035-1087 and King of England 
2 CONC 1066-1087. About one-fifth or one-sixth of William's 1066 invasion force was from outside Normandy, notably from Brittany, Flanders, Artois and Picardy.   K-1350: William I, Duke of Normandy and King of England, born 14 Oct. 1024 
2 CONC at Falais, Calvados, France; married Matilda about 1053; died 9 Sept. 1087 at Hermenbraville, S-Infr., France.   Norr lists six or seven children by Matilda: Adelia, William II, Henry I, Adelaide, Robert and Constance (and/or) Dau
2 CONC ghter, born about 1066. AF lists an Anna born about 1066. Others could be children of mistresses, not by Matilda.   He had several other children besides the five listed by Butler, Butler says. K. is the only one who lists Gundred
2 CONC  as a daughter. He could be wrong.
