2 CONC  feaudalism under which his followers were granted land in returnfor pledges of service and loyalty. As King William was noted for hisefficient if harsh rule. His administration relied upon Norman and other foreignpersonnell espec
2 CONC ially Lanfranc Archbishop of Canterbury. In 1085 startedDomesday Book
2 CONT
2 CONT AKA - Guillaume I "Le Conquaernt" de Normandie
2 CONT
