2 CONT The book, 'Kings & Queens of Great Britain'
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Cecilia of Normandy (or Cecily; c.1056 – 30 July 1126) possibly the eldest daughter of William the Conqueror and Matilda of Flanders. Her brothers were Kings William II of England and Henry I of England.  She was buried within the
2 CONC  walls of the Abbey of Sainte-Trinité at Caen. Her tomb is walled up without any opening being left through which it can be discovered.
