2 CONT Name Suffix:<NSFX> Princess of Eng. Ancestral File Number:<AFN> 8XJ0-3C Title: Princess Of ENGLAND and Countess of Blois. Death Place: Marsilly, Charente-Maritime, France.
2 CONT 1  NOTE became a Nun at Cluniac Priory in widowhood
2 CONT
2 CONT She became a Nun at Cluniac Priory in widowhood.
2 CONT Sources: RC 81, 299, 133; K and Q of Britain, Norr, A. Roots 139, 169; Kraentzler 1079, 1081, 1218, 1241; Ashley; AF.
2 CONT She was a nun when she died. Also called Adele, Adelia, Adelidis,Alice.
2 CONT Called Adele of Normandy, since she born there, and Adele of England,since she became Princess of England after 1066.
2 CONT K: Adela/Adele, Princess of England.
2 CONT Roots: Adela, born about 1062, died 1137, daughter of William theConqueror. Married about 1080, before 1085.
2 CONT Ashley: Adela, died 1137.
