2 CONT 2.         TANCRED of Sicily ([1119]-[1135/45]).  The Annals of Romoald name (in order) "Rogerium…Tancredum…Anfusium…Guillelmus, Heinricum, filiam unam" as the children of "rex Rogerius" & his first wife, specifying that Tancred w
2 CONC as Prince of Taranto[519].  Houben notes that Tancred was knighted with his older brother in Aug 1135 and suggests that this indicates they were both aged about 16, the normal age to be knighted[520].  The Chronicle of Romualdo Gu
2 CONC arna records that all the cities of Apulia swore homage to "dux…Rogerus…filiisque suis…Rogerio et Tancredo" in Sep 1130[521].  Principe di Bari 1135.  The Chronicle of Romualdo Guarna records the deaths of "Albyria…regina…et filia
2 CONC  eius…Tarentinus princeps et Anfusus Capuanorum princeps et Henricus", recorded in a section dealing with 1145 although the text appears to be recapitalitive of earlier events[522]. 
