1 CONT
1 CONT From Compton's:
1 CONT
1 CONT William I (born 1027, ruled 1066-87), called William the Conqueror, was
1 CONT an illegitimate son of Robert I, duke of Normandy. His mother was a
1 CONT tanner's daughter. William succeeded his father when he was only 7
1 CONT years old. At 24 he had made himself the mightiest feudal lord in all
1 CONT France by various conquests, but his ambition was not satisfied. He
1 CONT laid plans to become king of England also.  He was coronated at
1 CONT Westminster Abbey, Christmas Day 1066.
1 CONT    William married Matilda, daughter of Baldwin V, count of Flanders,
1 CONT in 1053. She was descended from the old Anglo-Saxon line of kings.
1 CONT Among their children were four sons: Robert, future duke of Normandy;
1 CONT Richard, who died as a youth; William Rufus, who succeeded his father
1 CONT as king of England; and Henry, who succeeded William Rufus. One
1 CONT daughter, Adela, became the mother of England's King Stephen.
1 CONT
