1 CONC ing or adopted daughter. However, this connection to William I has now been firmly debunked--see Gundred's discussion page for further information.
1 CONT
1 CONT Matilda was a seventh generation direct descendent of Alfred the Great. Her marriage to William strengthened his claim to the throne through her. Every sovereign of England is directly descended continously from her, including Que
1 CONC en Elizabeth II. 
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] References
1 CONT Her love for her husband is referenced in the Award-winning play, Angels in America.
1 CONT
1 CONT ^ Hilliam, Paul (2005). William the Conqueror: First Norman King of England. New York City, New York: Rosen Publishing Group, 20. ISBN 1-4042-0166-1.  
