1 CONC 0, Henry took advantage of the absence of another brother, Robert, who had a prior claim to the throne, to seize the royal treasury and have himself crowned king at Westminster. Henry subsequently secured his position with nobles 
1 CONC and with the church by issuing a charter of liberties favorable to them.  In 1101 Robert, who was duke of Normandy, invaded England, but Henry persuaded him to withdraw by promising him a pension and military aid.  In 1102, Henry 
1 CONC put down a revolt of nobles.
