0 @N6000000002187596358@ NOTE Robert I, Duke of Burgundy
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Robert I Capet (1011 – March 21, 1076) was duke of Burgundy between 1032 to his death. Robert was son of King Robert II of France and brother of Henry I.
1 CONT
1 CONT In 1025, with the death of his eldest brother Hugh Magnus, he and Henry rebelled against their father and defeated him, forcing him back to Paris. In 1031, after the death of his father the king, Robert participated in a rebellion
1 CONC  against his brother, in which he was supported by his mother, Queen Constance d'Arles. Peace was only achieved when Robert was given Burgundy (1032).
1 CONT
1 CONT Throughout his reign, he was little more than a robber baron who had no control over his own vassals, whose estates he often plundered, especially those of the Church. He seized the income of the diocese of Autun and the wine of t
1 CONC he canons of Dijon. He burgled the abbey of St-Germain at Auxerre. In 1055, he repudiated his wife, Helie of Semur, and assassinated her brother Joceran and murdered her father, his father-in-law, Lord Dalmace I of Semur, with his
1 CONC  own hands. In that same year, the bishop of Langres, Harduoin, refused to dedicate the church of Sennecy so as not "to be exposed to the violence of the duke."
1 CONT
1 CONT His first son, Hugh, died in battle at a young age and his second son, Henry, also predeceased him. He was succeeded by Henry's eldest son, his grandson, Hugh I.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit]
1 CONT Family
1 CONT He married his first wife, Helie of Semur, about 1033, and repudiated her in 1055. Robert and Helie had five children:
1 CONT
1 CONT Hugh (1034–1059), killed in battle 
1 CONT Henry (1035–ca.1074) 
1 CONT Robert (1040–1113), poisoned; married Violante of Sicily, daughter of Roger I of Sicily 
1 CONT Simon (1045–1087) 
1 CONT Constance (1046–1093), married Alfonso VI of Castile 
1 CONT From his second wife, Ermengarde of Anjou, daughter of Fulk III of Anjou, he had one daughter: 
1 CONT Hildegard (c.1056–1104), married Duke William VIII of Aquitaine 
1 CONT [edit]
1 CONT See also
1 CONT Dukes of Burgundy family tree 
1 CONT [edit]
1 CONT Sources
1 CONT Gwatking, H. M., Whitney, J. P., et al. Cambridge Medieval History: Volume III—Germany and the Western Empire. Cambridge University Press: London, 1930. 
0 @N6000000002322288638@ NOTE He was the younger brother to Henry, whom his mother, Constance, favored to
1 CONT succeed to the crown upon the death of their father, Robert II. When Robert
1 CONT II died in 1031, a civil war broke out and Henry sought refuge with Robert
1 CONT the Duke of Normandy, afterwhich Robert, the brother to Henry, was given
1 CONT Burgundy in 1032. Henry aided William, the furure William I of England,
1 CONT Robert's successor as Duke of Normandy, to quell his rebellious vassels in
1 CONT 1047, but was thereafter at war with him (the duke of Normandy). Confused??
